# SECRETS & manual setup — {{PRODUCT_NAME}}

> This is the **only** list of things a human must do. The agent has done
> everything else. Work top to bottom; each step says where to do it and which
> GitHub secret to paste the result into
> (repo → Settings → Secrets and variables → Actions → New repository secret).

## 1. Supabase
- [ ] Create a Supabase project (one for prod; optionally a second for staging).
      → https://supabase.com/dashboard
- [ ] Copy **Project URL** → secret `SUPABASE_URL`.
- [ ] Copy **anon/publishable key** → secret `SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY`.
- [ ] (If using a Worker/edge fn) copy **service_role key** → set as a Worker
      secret only (`wrangler secret put SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY --env <env>`),
      NEVER a client/web secret.
- [ ] Apply migrations: paste `supabase/migrations/*.sql` in the SQL editor, or
      `supabase db push` after linking.

## 2. Google sign-in
- [ ] Google Cloud Console → create OAuth 2.0 **Web** client.
      Authorized redirect URI: `https://<project-ref>.supabase.co/auth/v1/callback`.
- [ ] Paste **client id + secret** into Supabase → Authentication → Providers → Google.
- [ ] Supabase → Authentication → URL Configuration: add the prod + staging
      Pages URLs and `http://localhost:*`.

## 3. Cloudflare (web hosting)
- [ ] Create a Pages project named `{{PROJECT}}`. → https://dash.cloudflare.com
- [ ] Create an API token (Pages + Workers edit) → secret `CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN`.
- [ ] Copy your **Account ID** → secret `CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID`.
- [ ] Map domains: prod domain → `main` branch; `staging.<domain>` → `staging`.
- [ ] (If Worker) `wrangler secret put ... --env staging|production` for each secret.

## 4. Firebase App Distribution (Android)
- [ ] Create a Firebase project + register the Android app → copy the **App ID**
      → secret `FIREBASE_APP_ID`.
- [ ] Create a service account with the "Firebase App Distribution Admin" role,
      download the JSON key, paste its **full contents** → secret
      `FIREBASE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT`.
- [ ] App Distribution → create a tester group named `testers` (matches the workflow).

## 5. Stripe (only if payments enabled)
- [ ] Create a Stripe account. Use **test** keys for staging, **live** for prod.
- [ ] Worker secrets: `STRIPE_SECRET_KEY`, `STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET` per env.
- [ ] Add the webhook endpoint (the Worker/edge-fn URL) in the Stripe dashboard.

## 6. Branch protection (repo → Settings → Branches)
- [ ] Protect `main` and `staging`: require PR + passing `CI`, block force-push.

## 7. MCP env vars (let the agent run things — see `mcp/` + `secrets-manager`)
Set these as shell env vars (or your tool's user-scope MCP config); never commit
real values. Servers without a var set just stay disconnected.
- [ ] `GITHUB_PAT` — GitHub → Settings → Developer settings → tokens (repo + workflow).
- [ ] `SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN` — supabase.com/dashboard/account/tokens (personal token).
- [ ] `SUPABASE_PROJECT_REF` — Supabase Project Settings → General → Project ID
      (use the **staging** ref; the MCP defaults to read-only).
- [ ] `STRIPE_SECRET_KEY` — only if payments; use a restricted/test key.
- [ ] Cloudflare + Playwright + Context7 MCPs need no key (OAuth / none). On first
      Cloudflare use, approve the OAuth prompt in the browser.
- [ ] Restart Cursor after setting these (MCP config loads on launch).

---
When every box is checked, the pipeline is fully live: push to a `cursor/*`
branch → PR → merge to `staging` → run **Deploy Web** (staging) and
**Deploy Mobile** from the Actions tab. Promote to `main` for production.
